WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.329 --> 00:00:04.430
When it comes to films and television shows,
there's a lot riding on an actors' preparedness

00:00:04.430 --> 00:00:05.899
for a production.

00:00:05.899 --> 00:00:09.620
Even if all of the crew members show up primed
and ready to work, everything can fall apart

00:00:09.620 --> 00:00:11.950
if the cast doesn't quite have it together.

00:00:11.950 --> 00:00:15.589
These stars got creative and engaged in some
last-minute scrambling to make up for the

00:00:15.589 --> 00:00:19.910
fact that they weren't quite prepared for
their roles when they signed on.

00:00:19.910 --> 00:00:21.560
Big Momma's coma

00:00:21.560 --> 00:00:26.570
In 1999, the world almost lost Martin Lawrence
when the actor collapsed and fell into a coma

00:00:26.570 --> 00:00:30.039
outside his L.A. home due to severe heat-related
exhaustion.

00:00:30.039 --> 00:00:34.180
Lawrence's condition was so serious that for
several days he required a ventilator just

00:00:34.180 --> 00:00:35.250
to breathe.

00:00:35.250 --> 00:00:39.250
It all happened largely because he chose to
work out while wearing a big plastic suit

00:00:39.250 --> 00:00:43.100
in 100-degree weather to try and get in shape
for Big Momma's House.

00:00:43.100 --> 00:00:46.580
"Please, I recommend do not run in a plastic
suit.

00:00:46.580 --> 00:00:47.780
Do not do that."

00:00:47.780 --> 00:00:52.120
Luckily, he went on to make a full recovery,
but the media criticized Lawrence's decision

00:00:52.120 --> 00:00:56.200
to get in shape since he wouldn't have many
opportunities to show off his abs in costume

00:00:56.200 --> 00:00:57.200
anyway.

00:00:57.200 --> 00:01:01.511
But walking around in an 80-pound bodysuit
still required some fitness preparation, even

00:01:01.511 --> 00:01:03.700
if Lawrence took it too far.

00:01:03.700 --> 00:01:05.340
Tuned out

00:01:05.340 --> 00:01:09.100
Prior to physically appearing in the Marvel
Cinematic Universe as Vision, Paul Bettany

00:01:09.100 --> 00:01:13.260
never bothered to watch a single film in the
Iron Man franchise, despite providing the

00:01:13.260 --> 00:01:16.450
vocals for Jarvis, the hero's trusty AI sidekick.

00:01:16.450 --> 00:01:18.220
"Miss Potts is approaching.

00:01:18.220 --> 00:01:19.160
I recommend that you…"

00:01:19.160 --> 00:01:20.160
"MUTE!"

00:01:20.360 --> 00:01:24.420
Even when he was recording his lines as Jarvis,
Bettany didn't even get a full version of

00:01:24.420 --> 00:01:27.700
the script and had no context for the dialogue
pieces he read.

00:01:27.700 --> 00:01:31.500
"As Jarvis, I would turn up at the end of

00:01:31.500 --> 00:01:36.340
the movie and speak into a microphone for
two hours and they'd give me a big whopping,

00:01:36.340 --> 00:01:37.600
great bag of cash."

00:01:37.600 --> 00:01:42.400
Bettany's indifference to the franchise was
such that he admitted to feeling like a "pirate"

00:01:42.400 --> 00:01:46.630
when he took his money, and often had to tell
fans he had no idea who the character was

00:01:46.630 --> 00:01:50.970
when he was approached to speak about what
is now one of his most famous roles.

00:01:50.970 --> 00:01:52.390
Liquid courage

00:01:52.390 --> 00:01:56.290
Undressing in front of one person is hard
enough, so it's gotta be especially awkward

00:01:56.290 --> 00:02:00.330
for an actor to strip on camera, with a whole
crew watching from the wings.

00:02:00.330 --> 00:02:04.290
For Margot Robbie, her breakout role in The
Wolf of Wall Street called for her to be in

00:02:04.290 --> 00:02:08.299
the buff quite a bit, and she knew the shots
would be ruined if her nervousness came through

00:02:08.299 --> 00:02:09.399
on-camera.

00:02:09.399 --> 00:02:14.270
With little time to prepare herself for one
scene of extreme exposure, decided to do what

00:02:14.270 --> 00:02:18.560
a lot of people might do for a confidence
boost, and pounded three shots of tequila

00:02:18.560 --> 00:02:21.459
before stripping down and nailing the scene
in one take.

00:02:21.459 --> 00:02:25.459
Meanwhile, co-stars Leonardo DiCaprio and
Jonah Hill weren't very familiar with the

00:02:25.459 --> 00:02:29.480
effects of most of the drugs they were supposed
to pretend to take on-screen, so both had

00:02:29.480 --> 00:02:32.480
to be coached on how to act convincingly high.

00:02:33.420 --> 00:02:34.500
"Steve."

00:02:34.500 --> 00:02:35.660
"STEEEVE."

00:02:36.360 --> 00:02:40.920
In fact, DiCaprio was so unsure about how
to act, he'd later admit that he spent hours

00:02:40.930 --> 00:02:45.440
watching this YouTube video of a guy drunkenly
rolling around on the floor to better shape

00:02:45.440 --> 00:02:47.310
his performance.

00:02:47.310 --> 00:02:48.640
Learning the lingo

00:02:48.640 --> 00:02:53.010
When Jackie Chan first arrived in the U.S.
in the 1980s, he was reportedly unable to

00:02:53.010 --> 00:02:57.670
speak even basic English and quickly set about
teaching himself how to communicate by absorbing

00:02:57.670 --> 00:02:58.670
Western media.

00:02:58.670 --> 00:03:02.870
He came to America alone to "immerse himself
in the English-speaking world" and learn the

00:03:02.870 --> 00:03:04.390
language that way.

00:03:04.390 --> 00:03:08.040
Although Chan did pick up on English pretty
well over the years, he still had trouble

00:03:08.040 --> 00:03:12.380
reading scripts as late as the Rush Hour series
and had to learn the lines for many of his

00:03:12.380 --> 00:03:13.450
Western films phonetically.

00:03:14.880 --> 00:03:19.440
"Do you understand the words that are coming
out of my mouth?"

00:03:20.160 --> 00:03:23.920
Sometimes, crews would take advantage of this
and make Chan say swear words or things he

00:03:23.920 --> 00:03:25.880
didn't mean, just for laughs.

00:03:25.880 --> 00:03:27.190
"I'm into feet.

00:03:27.190 --> 00:03:29.240
I like the one with the horses.

00:03:29.240 --> 00:03:30.600
What's that mean?

00:03:30.620 --> 00:03:32.420
What he teach me?"

00:03:33.060 --> 00:03:34.760
Doing dialect

00:03:34.760 --> 00:03:38.430
Most of the actors in Games of Thrones have
accents based on where in the fictional world

00:03:38.430 --> 00:03:42.700
of Westeros they hail from, relative to the
geography of the U.K.

00:03:42.700 --> 00:03:46.940
For example, characters hailing from the North
have thick Northern accents, whereas those

00:03:46.940 --> 00:03:50.970
from the south speak with accents commonly
found in the more southerly parts of the U.K.

00:03:50.970 --> 00:03:55.060
Production was reportedly insistent that the
actors playing the sons of Ned Stark should

00:03:55.060 --> 00:03:59.879
adopt Sean Bean's native Yorkshire accent,
but Kit Harington had no idea that this would

00:03:59.879 --> 00:04:03.690
be expected of him and auditioned for the
role of Jon Snow in his native southern accent.

00:04:03.690 --> 00:04:07.769
Although he was told he was a good match for
the character, he still needed to speak more

00:04:07.769 --> 00:04:10.450
like his on-screen dad before the cameras
started rolling.

00:04:10.450 --> 00:04:14.629
So Harington—along with the rest of the
actors expected to portray Ned Stark's sons—had

00:04:14.629 --> 00:04:19.529
to rush to ready their new dialects to match
their daddy's off-screen affectation.

00:04:19.529 --> 00:04:20.620
Getting ripped

00:04:20.620 --> 00:04:26.159
Upon being cast to play infamous British criminal
Charles Bronson, a man so dangerously violent

00:04:26.159 --> 00:04:30.419
and superhumanly built he once punched clean
through bulletproof glass in a fit of anger,

00:04:30.419 --> 00:04:34.560
Tom Hardy met with the man himself to see
if he'd sign off his portrayal.

00:04:34.560 --> 00:04:38.759
Bronson was unimpressed with Hardy's physique,
however, and initially said no.

00:04:38.759 --> 00:04:43.039
Hoping to change Bronson's mind, Hardy started
bulking up after their first meeting, consuming

00:04:43.039 --> 00:04:47.689
nothing but pizza, ice cream, chicken and
rice while exercising as hard as he could.

00:04:47.689 --> 00:04:51.620
Two weeks later, he'd bulked up enough for
Bronson to realize he was committed to physically

00:04:51.620 --> 00:04:52.729
portraying him.

00:04:52.729 --> 00:04:56.870
The fact that Hardy also brought Bronson a
muffin and some milkshakes also likely didn't

00:04:56.870 --> 00:04:57.870
hurt.

00:04:57.870 --> 00:05:01.810
Along with giving the actor his blessing,
Bronson also shaved off his mustache and mailed

00:05:01.810 --> 00:05:05.900
it to Hardy, hoping the makeup department
could figure out a way to glue it to his face.

00:05:05.900 --> 00:05:09.860
Failing that, Bronson hoped Hardy could carry
the clippings around in his pocket as a good

00:05:09.860 --> 00:05:10.860
luck charm.

00:05:10.860 --> 00:05:13.419
It's unclear which option Hardy chose.

00:05:13.419 --> 00:05:14.490
Thanks for watching!

